FUN_0000_e3bc: thread the screen-descriptor cx:bx into the (*c564)() = FUN_0000_0340 method call.

e3bc paints a screen via the video-driver method vector DGROUP:0x564 (= MGAVIDEO FUN_0000_0340, the
menu-background render).  asm 0xe3e2: `mov bx,0xf6cc ; mov cx,ds ; call FAR [DGROUP:0x564]` -- cx:bx is
the on-screen descriptor at DGROUP:0xf6cc (ds = DGROUP = 0x1c00 -> linear 0x2b6cc).  The __allregs
indirect method-vector site dropped cx:bx (only unaff_CS was passed), so 0340 got a garbage descriptor
pointer (~g_mem-0xEC) and NULL-deref'd on its palette copy.  Thread it faithfully: 0340's C signature is
(param_1 = the descriptor segment cx, param_2 = the descriptor pointer); 0340 uses only *param_2 = the
descriptor's first word (its resource segment).  Descriptor pointer = g_mem + (0x1c00<<4) + 0xf6cc =
g_mem + 0x2b6cc.  (Per-patch indirect-call arg threading, per CLAUDE.md; the c564 vector stably resolves
to 0340 on this path.)  Asm-verified 0xe3e2..0xe3e7.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -33581,7 +33581,10 @@
     DAT_2000_b6ce = bVar1;
     FUN_0000_e3f8();
   }
-  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c564)))(unaff_CS);
+  /* PATCH 094: thread the descriptor cx:bx=0x1c00:0xf6cc (g_mem+0x2b6cc) into the (*c564)()=0340
+     menu-background render; the __allregs vector site had dropped it -> garbage descriptor -> SIGSEGV. */
+  ((void (*)(undefined2, undefined2 *))fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c564)))
+      (0x1c00, (undefined2 *)(g_mem + 0x2b6cc));
   DAT_2000_b6c0 = 1;
   DAT_2000_b6c2 = 0xffff;
   return;
